msgstr "On 4K jack charts the bonus above the bar is halved, since very high accuracy is normal there."

#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "On 4K the slices come from the play's own MSD skillset ratings, bucketed by whichever skillset is strongest on that chart: jack (JackSpeed and Chordjack), tech (Technical and Jumpstream), speed (Stream) and stamina (Handstream and Stamina). Jumpstream sits with tech on purpose. MinaCalc's Jumpstream fires hard on dense jumptrill, which feels a lot more like tech than like speed, so pairing it with Stream put charts like Blastix Riotz [GRAVITY] on a tile labelled speed. Checked against a 25 chart pack of real gamma speed charts, Stream alone picks all 25 and rejects the jumptrill charts by a wide margin."
#~ msgstr "On 4K the slices come from the play's own MSD skillset ratings, bucketed by whichever skillset is strongest on that chart: jack (JackSpeed and Chordjack), tech (Technical and Jumpstream), speed (Stream) and stamina (Handstream and Stamina). Jumpstream sits with tech on purpose. MinaCalc's Jumpstream fires hard on dense jumptrill, which feels a lot more like tech than like speed, so pairing it with Stream put charts like Blastix Riotz [GRAVITY] on a tile labelled speed. Checked against a 25 chart pack of real gamma speed charts, Stream alone picks all 25 and rejects the jumptrill charts by a wide margin."

#: src/components/prism/PrismUpdates.tsx
#~ msgid "On a chart under OD 5, pressing every key on a steady beat can score close to playing the notes. Prism now checks that, and rates a section as mashed when mashing it scores higher than playing it at the chart's level. Charts at OD 5 and up are not checked."
#~ msgstr "On a chart under OD 5, pressing every key on a steady beat can score close to playing the notes. Prism now checks that, and rates a section as mashed when mashing it scores higher than playing it at the chart's level. Charts at OD 5 and up are not checked."

#: src/components/me/GoalsPanel.tsx
#~ msgid "on a map"
#~ msgstr "on a map"

#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "On dense charts Stream and Technical often rate within a fraction of each other, and whichever edges ahead is close to a coin flip. Speed normally wins those near-ties, but when Technical sits that close and the chart analysis itself is confident the chart is tech, the pass files under tech instead."
#~ msgstr "On dense charts Stream and Technical often rate within a fraction of each other, and whichever edges ahead is close to a coin flip. Speed normally wins those near-ties, but when Technical sits that close and the chart analysis itself is confident the chart is tech, the pass files under tech instead."

#: src/components/prism/PrismUpdates.tsx
msgid "On low OD charts the hit windows are wide enough that pressing every key on a steady beat still hits most of the notes. Prism now judges that mash against the chart's hit windows, and when a section mashed gets 90% or more while being much easier than reading it, the section is rated as the mash."
msgstr "On low OD charts the hit windows are wide enough that pressing every key on a steady beat still hits most of the notes. Prism now judges that mash against the chart's hit windows, and when a section mashed gets 90% or more while being much easier than reading it, the section is rated as the mash."

