#: src/components/prism/PrismUpdates.tsx
#~ msgid "Prism filed three chord rows in a row as a bracket whenever none shared a key with the one before it, so a roll of three split shapes counted too. The third row now has to come back to a key of the first, as in a real bracket, and the rows that don't are Chordstream."
#~ msgstr "Prism filed three chord rows in a row as a bracket whenever none shared a key with the one before it, so a roll of three split shapes counted too. The third row now has to come back to a key of the first, as in a real bracket, and the rows that don't are Chordstream."

#: src/components/prism/PrismUpdates.tsx
msgid "Prism filed three chord rows in a row as a bracket whenever none shared a key with the one before it, so a roll of three split shapes counted too. The third row now has to come back to a key of the first, as in a real bracket, and the rows that don't are Chordstream. A hand hitting the same chord again within 250ms, with the other hand playing in between, is a jack."
msgstr "Prism filed three chord rows in a row as a bracket whenever none shared a key with the one before it, so a roll of three split shapes counted too. The third row now has to come back to a key of the first, as in a real bracket, and the rows that don't are Chordstream. A hand hitting the same chord again within 250ms, with the other hand playing in between, is a jack."

